**`ErrorBoundary.tsx`** — usage:

```tsx
// Basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={<p>Oops!</p>}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` triggers the fallback render
- `componentDidCatch` logs error + component stack to console
- `retry` resets state, letting React re-mount children
- `fallback` prop overrides default UI when provided
